li-ii-p2 = prose (cons "Tversky and Kahneman made description invariance a normative axiom of rational choice: two descriptions of the same prospect are the same option, and the choice must not depend on which is shown (Science 1981; Journal of Business 1986). The typical human breaks it systematically. De Martino et al. located the break in the amygdala, an affect heuristic firing on the wording (Science 2006). Autistic subjects were largely invariant, and their skin conductance did not separate the frames (Journal of Neuroscience 2008)." nil)
